Pex (Program Exploration eXtension) is a programatic code property-based testing tool in .NET. This tool generates a variety of test data and drives a program on that test data to test if the program returns correct results and doesn’t have any side-effects. This tool helps identify and fix flaws in code and libraries by generating a broad range of test cases automatically.

The "Microsoft Pex Framework" project supports both Microsoft .NET and open-source .NET projects. The Pex framework applies well under various development scenarios, including continuous integration, exploratory design, exploratory testing, and exploratory debugging. It helps in identifying hidden bugs, generating new test cases, and improving the test suite. -->

